<title>GERMANY: Siemens to build Taiwan power plant.</title>
<headline>Siemens to build Taiwan power plant.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering group Siemens AG said on Monday it had won an order for the turnkey construction of a gas turbine power plant in Taiwan worth 110 million marks.</p>
<p>Siemens said in a statement that the twin-block plant, to be built near the capital Taipei for the Taiwan Power Company, would have a total capacity of 296 megawatts.</p>
<p>Construction is expected to take 18 months.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
